            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My kids thought this was awesome. I didn't have a cinnamon stick so I just used about a 1/4 tsp. cinnamon. I also used organic unsweetened coconut. They inhaled it and asked for seconds. Smart way to use flax seed! (This was two servings for my kids, BTW.)",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-17T08:15:36.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alberta Rose"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty, healthy and quick way to change up the breakfast routine. I followed this recipe, using a mix of frozen berries/fruit. The brown sugar made a nice glaze with just enough sweetness. I used a toasted flax meal to add some nut flavor. The cinnamon flavor got lost, so I would use regular ground cinnamon instead of the stick. I also might toast the coconut. It added interest and crunch, but the flavor wasn't there. Thanks for sharing this recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-11T07:49:51.630Z"
          }
